0.6.0

* Cached gating sequence: publishers rescan consumers only when a
  claim would wrap the ring.
* Multi-producer publish uses an available[] buffer so commits are
  independent; max_read_cursor is advanced over the contiguous run.
* Single-producer sequencer (sp_publisher_*): no fetch-add, release
  store on commit.
* Batch claim: publisher_next_entries_* and sp_publisher_next_entries_*.
* Wait strategy rechecks the condition every DISRUPTOR_PAUSE_SPINS
  pauses instead of spinning 5120 times blindly, then yields.
* Sequences padded to two cache lines (Intel adjacent-line prefetch).
* DEFINE_ENTRY_TYPE no longer pads every slot; DEFINE_PADDED_ENTRY_TYPE
  keeps the old layout.
* Consumer cursor release uses __ATOMIC_RELEASE.
* Portable CPU pause (x86 PAUSE, ARM YIELD).
